# The optional enhancements' hook points in the levels' own (transliterated) copies of the hero functions.
#
# The hand ports of Veldin's hero code (and Novalis's, the *_l1.cpp files) call src/game/enhance/advanced.h at the points
# where R&C 3's movement, the strafe and the modern aim differ from the original. Rilgar (L5),
# Blarg's Nebula G34 (L6), Batalia (L8), Pokitaru (L11), Drek's fleet (L17) and Veldin's finale (L18) run their own builds of those functions, machine-transliterated
# (rilgar_hero_tr_*.cpp, blarg_hero_tr_*.cpp, batalia_hero_tr_*.cpp, pokitaru_hero_tr_*.cpp, veldin_orbit_hero_tr_*.cpp,
# veldin_finale_hero_tr_*.cpp): the generator puts the same
# calls there, at the instruction of the level's own code that corresponds to the hand port's point (the alignment of the
# two instruction streams).
#
# Read by tools/codegen/mips2cpp.py (load_hooks; mkall.py sets MIPS2CPP_HOOKS to this file):
#   L<n> 0xADDR: <statement>   emitted before the instruction at ADDR of level n's code, after its label
#   L<n> 0xADDR label          ADDR made a label, for a statement's `goto L_<addr>`
# With every enhancement off each statement is a test that fails (advanced_rac3_movement(), advanced_strafe_flip(), ...):
# the code then runs as transliterated. Registers: the player block 0x13f350 is `<base> - 0xcb0` (a level's base register
# is named in each line); `goto` targets are labels of the function.
#
# Veldin's points (0x217970 hero_state_update, 0x2223f8 hero_set_state, 0x229b70 hero_input_update, 0x214658
# hero_horizontal_velocity, 0x211be8 hero_stick_speed), the hand ports' calls:
#   A  0x21c000  run_update: R&C 3's "move along the stick" flag (advanced_rac3_along_stick), the original's rule skipped (to 0x21c0a4)
#   B  0x21c168  run_update: R&C 3's turn springs (advanced_rac3_run_turn: f20, the acceleration factor), the original's turn skipped (to 0x21c2dc)
#   C  0x21c308  run_update: the acceleration / deceleration factors 7.5 / 8.5 (f0 / f1) -> R&C 3's 37 / 30
#   D  0x225790  enter_jump (the jump states' entry): advanced_rac3_jump before the 0x490 default
#   E  0x22f2d4  run_jump: R&C 3's running jump rule (a0 = 9 / 7 for hero_set_state at 0x231c10)
#   F  0x22b568  run_input: the strafe flip (state 0xb) instead of the jump, then the function's end (0x231c4c)
#   G  0x22b968  run_input: R&C 3's stop (advanced_rac3_stop), then the original's standing path at 0x22ba70 (no skid, no 25 frames)
#   H  0x22b390  swing_input: running out of a swing / the throw (advanced_rac3_swing_exit, s1 the combo row)
#   I  0x2149c4  hero_horizontal_velocity, states 0xb / 0xc: the strafe flip's speed (to 0x214a58)
#   J  0x214de0  hero_horizontal_velocity: R&C 3's air braking (f12 = k x 8 / 11, k = f4) instead of 2 / 6
#   K  after each call of the level's own hero_stick_speed (Blarg, Pokitaru): advanced_move_speed, as hero_stick_speed (ovl_21.cpp)
#   L  0x227fa0  hero_item_use, after its +0x1090 test: no item input while the thrown wrench is out (advanced_rac3_wrench_out; to the return 0)
#   M  0x22c45c  crouch_input (state 4): the crouch throw 0x15 skipped while the thrown wrench is out (to the instruction after the call)

