# ---- Points I / J in the PAL build (SCES-50916) of hero_horizontal_velocity, for the stand-ins generated from the PAL disc
# (tools/codegen/ovlist.py: the PAL build changed this function, its NTSC-U code is not on that disc). `L<n> PAL:0xADDR` is an
# address of the PAL build's code and `L_PAL_<addr>` a label there; tools/codegen/mkall.py moves both to the stand-in's
# addresses. Each point is the instruction that corresponds to the NTSC-U point above (the code around it, from the
# point to its goto target, is the same in both builds; the PAL build adds its hero sound 1 call before point I).
